// std/magnitude.dag -- Terminal opaque carrier for unbounded counting.
//
// Magnitude is the foot of the construction chain
//   Magnitude → Nat → Int → Rational → Real
// (R3 lane #6, T-Numeric-Construction). Modeling discipline: construction-chain
// layer authority is this module plus dsl/std/nat.dag, integer.dag, rational.dag.
//
// SHAPE: opaque atom — no fields, no algebra inhabitance, no value body.
// Refinements `Nat<N>` / `Int<N>` (later slices) parameterize the namespace
// to give it concrete bit-width at grounding time. Magnitude itself carries
// no width — that is the structurally honest representation of "unbounded
// counting." Encoding design: abstract counting, rejecting bit-stream and
// word-stream encodings (no storage encoding at this layer).
//
// PRECEDENT: `dsl/std/constructors.dag:68,72` declares `type Product` and
// `type Coproduct` as bare opaque atoms — same shape as Magnitude.
//
// CONSUMERS: none in this slice. `Nat = Semiring<Magnitude>` and downstream
// chain layers land in subsequent slices per design doc §6 sequencing.
//
// HARD BOUNDARIES (per dispatch on inbox #1288):
//   - Not a parallel magnitude representation; this IS the canonical carrier.
//   - No tokenizer / `LitInt` / literal-grammar changes here.
//   - Not a migration of `dsl/std/integer.dag`'s `OrderedRing<Word64>` chain;
//     consumer migration is design doc §6 (later slice).

module std.magnitude

type Magnitude
